From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.networking.hostname/connectivity: HostName properties, profile name (3552)

windows.networking.hostname / connectivity: HostName properties, inspectable methods, profile name

IHostName: DisplayName, CanonicalName (lowercase names, normal form for IPv4/IPv6 addresses), Type
(domain / IPv4 / IPv6), IsEqual (by canonical name), IPInformation (NULL: only local adapters carry it).
The HostName factory, the HostName object, the NetworkInformation factory and ConnectionProfile answer
GetIids / GetRuntimeClassName / GetTrustLevel (BaseTrust). IConnectionProfile::ProfileName is the name of the
first connected network. DllGetClassObject for the two DLLs no longer logs a FIXME (they have no COM classes).
